  "notes": "West's heart lead is won by South. South's only possible problem is the loss of 2 trump tricks. This common card combination is often misplayed.\n\nThe correct play is to lead any spade (including the ♠Q) out of the closed hand and, if West follows small, play low from dummy. On the given lie of the cards, South is immediately successful.\n\nIf East is able to win the trick cheaply, South wins the return and takes a second spade finesse. If East discards, South can take a third spade finesse. The last trump is drawn and South easily takes the balance.\n\nRemember, when playing a 4-4 fit missing just the King and Jack for 1 loser, the best play is to double finesse.",
